          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nIn this example we show that the local ring <MATH_0001> has to be\na G-ring in order for the result of Lemma <REF_0001> to\nbe true. Namely, let <MATH_0002> be a Noetherian ring and let <MATH_0003>\nbe a maximal ideal of <MATH_0004>. Set <MATH_0005>. Let\n<MATH_0006> be a factorization with <MATH_0007> of finite type over\n<MATH_0008>. Set <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>, and\n<MATH_0011>. Consider the functor\n<MATH_0012> defined by the rule\n<MATHSEG_0001>if <MATHSEG_0002>\nLet <MATH_0013> is the category fibred in sets associated\nto <MATH_0014>, see Algebraic Stacks, Section <REF_0002>.\nThen <MATH_0015> is limit preserving on objects and\nthere exists an effective, versal formal object <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>.\nHence if the conclusion of Lemma <REF_0003> holds\nfor <MATH_0018>, then there exists a finite type ring map <MATH_0019>\nand a maximal ideal <MATH_0020> lying over <MATH_0021> such that\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0022>,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0023> and <MATH_0024> satisfy condition (4) of\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> there exists a <MATH_0025>-algebra map <MATH_0026>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nThus <MATH_0027> is smooth at <MATH_0028> by the lemma cited.\nSlicing <MATH_0029> we may assume that <MATH_0030> is <ACCENT_0001>tale at\n<MATH_0031>, see for example\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0005>\nor argue directly. Write <MATH_0032>.\nThen <MATH_0033> corresponds to a solution in <MATH_0034> of the system of equations\n<MATH_0035>, see Smoothing Ring Maps, Section\n<REF_0006>.\nThus if the conclusion of\nLemma <REF_0007> holds for every <MATH_0036> as\nabove, then a system of equations which has a solution in <MATH_0037> has a\nsolution in the henselization of <MATH_0038>.\nIn other words, the approximation property holds for\n<MATH_0039>. This implies that <MATH_0040>\nis a G-ring (insert future reference here; see also discussion in\nSmoothing Ring Maps, Section <REF_0008>)\nwhich in turn implies that <MATH_0041> is a G-ring.\n<STRUCT_0007>",
