      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Let <MATH_0002> be a category\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0003>. We say <MATH_0004> satisfies\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>openness of versality<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if given a scheme <MATH_0005> locally of finite type\nover <MATH_0006>, an object <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> over <MATH_0009>, and a finite type point\n<MATH_0010> such that <MATH_0011> is versal at <MATH_0012>, then there exists an open\nneighbourhood <MATH_0013> such that <MATH_0014> is versal at every finite\ntype point of <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0016> be a <MATH_0017>-morphism of categories\nfibred in groupoids over <MATH_0018>. We say <MATH_0019> satisfies\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>openness of versality<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if given a scheme <MATH_0020> locally of finite type\nover <MATH_0021>, an object <MATH_0022> of <MATH_0023> over <MATH_0024>, openness\nof versality holds for\n<MATH_0025>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:e07c25d147183c84cf6024605a6d58a09edc19345d2856ef29a6306359a10e83",
      "unit_id": "tag:07XQ:statement"
    },
